## Overview
All database interactions involving user-supplied input must strictly use parameterized queries, prepared statements, or ORM criteria builders. Dynamic SQL string concatenation or string formatting is strictly forbidden.

### Approved Java Spring Pattern
```java
// CORRECT: Parameterized Prepared Query
@Query("SELECT u FROM Account u WHERE u.accountNumber = :accountNum AND u.status = :status")
Optional<Account> findActiveAccount(@Param("accountNum") String accountNum, @Param("status") AccountStatus status);
```

### Forbidden Pattern
```java
// VULNERABLE: Direct String Concatenation
String query = "SELECT * FROM accounts WHERE id = '" + userInput + "'";
```

### Verification Gate
Before resolving an SQLi ticket, the developer must attach a clean Checkmarx SAST scan report and provide passing unit test fixtures.
